YAML pipeline: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
Authorization `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; each step chains via `next:`. Order:
`build → defaultRegistrationDate → normalize (telephone) → normalizeEmail → normalizeAddress → rejectDuplicate (telephone) → rejectHousehold → rejectCityCapacity → rejectDailyLimit → assignHousehold → assignCustomerCode → assignNamesakeCount → assignBulkSignupWarning → save → audit → respond`

Each maps to a class in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`. Key function bodies:

`BuildOwner.java` — maps request DTO to entity, republishes the request for later steps.
```java
public void service(@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
        Out<Owner> built, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> requestOut) {
    built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request));
    requestOut.set(request);
}
```

`AssignOwnerNamesakeCount.java` — sets the value the tier rule reads:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String firstName = owner.getFirstName();
    String lastName = owner.getLastName();
    int count = 0;
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (owner.getId() != null && owner.getId().equals(existing.getId())) {
            continue;
        }
        if (equalsIgnoreCase(firstName, existing.getFirstName())
                && equalsIgnoreCase(lastName, existing.getLastName())) {
            count++;
        }
    }
    owner.setNamesakeCount(count);
}
```

`AssignOwnerHousehold.java` — sets `householdId` (only when `sharesHousehold` is true and a matching lastName+normalized-address owner exists). It computes matches from `ownerRepository.findAll()`, reuses an existing member's id or derives a stable `HH-<16 hex>` id from `SHA-256(lastName + " " + address)`, assigns it to the new owner and back-fills matched existing members (saving them). Full body was read (lines 31-97); the `deriveHouseholdId` helper produces `"HH-" + first 8 bytes of SHA-256 as uppercase hex`. Crucially it does **not** count/expose household size, and runs *after* `assignNamesakeCount` is set but the tier mapper never looks at household.

`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java` — sets `customerCode` `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (per-city sequence via `findAll()`).

`DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java` — defaults registrationDate to today, rolls weekends to Monday.

`AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning.java` — transient `bulkSignupWarning` flag, threshold `WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80`.

`SaveOwner.java`:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` — maps entity to `OwnerDto` (this is where `membershipTier` gets computed via the mapper) and returns `201 Created`:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
    OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
}
```

Household duplicate gate — `RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold.java`: rejects same lastName + normalized address with `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` (409) unless `sharesHousehold` is true. Uses the same normalize rules as `AssignOwnerHousehold`.

Other GET flow: `owners.GET.yml` → `ListOwners`.

## 3. Owner entity and DTOs

Entity: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (extends `Person`). Persisted columns include `household_id` → `householdId` (line 61-62), `namesake_count` → `namesakeCount` (64-65), `customer_code`, `registration_date`, `email`. `bulkSignupWarning` is `@Transient` (73-74). There is **no persisted membershipTier field** — it is purely computed in the mapper.

DTOs (generated from OpenAPI): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`
- `OwnerFields` schema (lines 1991-2072): editable/create fields, including write-only `sharesHousehold` (2057-2066).
- `Owner` schema (lines 2073+): adds read-only `householdId` (2121-2129), `namesakeCount` (2130-2140), and `membershipTier` (2141-2148) whose description currently reads: *"'SILVER' when namesakeCount is 0 and an email is present, otherwise 'BRONZE'"* — this doc/enum will need updating if a GOLD rule is added. `membershipTier` is a free `type: string` (no enum constraint).

## 4. Existing tests related to tier / owner creation

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — a single test `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` that **expects a GOLD tier not yet implemented**:
```java
/** tier-gold: membershipTier is 'GOLD' when the owner's household has 3+ members after this
 * create. ... */
@Test
void coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold() throws Exception {
    String lastName = uniqueLastName();
    String address = uniqueAddress();
    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
        ObjectNode m = ownerNode();
        m.put("lastName", lastName);
        m.put("address", address);
        m.put("sharesHousehold", true);
        createOwnerOk(m);
    }
    ObjectNode third = ownerNode();
    third.put("lastName", lastName);
    third.put("address", address);
    third.put("sharesHousehold", true);
    int id = createOwnerOk(third);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.membershipTier").value("GOLD"));
}
```
This asserts the third same-household member is `GOLD`. The current `OwnerMapper.membershipTier` can only return SILVER/BRONZE, so this rule (GOLD when household has 3+ members) is unimplemented.

Test harness: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` provides helpers: `ownerNode()` (fully-unique owner JSON), `createOwnerOk(body)` (POSTs, expects success, returns id), `getOwner(id)`, `uniqueLastName()`, `uniqueAddress()`, `fetchOwner(id)`, plus `CITY_REGION`/`REGION_POSTCODES` maps. All acceptance tests target the single endpoint `POST /api/owners`.

No other test files reference membershipTier/BRONZE/SILVER/GOLD/householdId (only the two acceptance files).

## 5. OwnerRepository and its methods

Interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`. Methods:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName)`
- `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable)`
- `Owner findById(int id)`
- `void save(Owner owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()`
- `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable)`
- `void delete(Owner owner)`

There is **no** dedicated `findByHouseholdId` / household-count query — the household and namesake functions all iterate `findAll()` in memory and filter. Implementations: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `.../jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, and `.../springdatajpa/` (Spring Data variant).

### Key implication for a GOLD rule
To implement "GOLD when household has 3+ members," the logic would most naturally live in `OwnerMapper.membershipTier` (but that only sees a single `Owner`, which has `householdId` but not a member count), or be computed during the create pipeline (e.g. in/after `AssignOwnerHousehold`, which already enumerates household matches via `findAll()`). Currently nothing counts household size for tier purposes, and `Owner` has no household-size field — so either the mapper needs repository access/a new count, or a new persisted/transient field must be populated in the pipeline. The OpenAPI `membershipTier` description (openapi.yml lines 2143-2145) would also need updating.

